  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through next Tuesday) \nIssued at 1055 PM CDT Mon Aug 24 2026\n\nThe upper-level ridge will shift westward mid week, opening the \ndoor for a series of weak shortwave troughs to track southward \nacross the area. This will provide us with a brief stint of \nnortherly flow and some potential for isolated to scattered \nshowers and thunderstorms as early as Wednesday night, and \npotentially into Friday. These storms are not likely to be severe \nbut some gusty winds are always possible with convection during \nthe summer months.\n\nWith the cloud cover in place and a weak surface boundary pushing\nthrough the area, highs on Thursday will be a little cooler. This\nmay be Abilene's chance to break the consecutive 100 degree\nstreak. After that, dry conditions return as the high pressure\nridge builds back once again. May not be hitting 105+ like this\nlast week, but highs near or a few degrees above the 100 degree\nmark look likely into early next week.",
